ion of OpenSSH, GPUStack, FreeSWITCH, and IBM Flaws</title><link>https://thehackernews.com/2026/11/cisa-warns-of-active-exploitation-of.html</link><guid isPermaLink="false">urn:sha256:4703b2a7b4d7d2a2a912c1f3b529a5dedc5e64790d69ffd02c7609f716ee7f5d</guid><category>NEWS</category><chr2:sourceName>The Hacker News</chr2:sourceName><chr2:firstObservedAtJST>2026-11-10T16:22:41.247857+09:00</chr2:firstObservedAtJST><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 06:31:42 GMT</pubDate><description>The U.S. Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) on Monday added four security flaws impacting GPUStack, SignalWire FreeSwitch, OpenBSD OpenSSH, and IBM Aspera Faspex to its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) catalog, citing evidence of active exploitation. The vulnerabilities are listed below - CVE-2026-123218 (CVSS score: 9.8) - An incorrect authorization vulnerability</description><chr2:heatScore>75.0</chr2:heatScore></item><item><title>N-able Takes N-central Cloud Offline After Researcher Discloses 33 Zero-Days with PoC Exploits</title><link>https://thehackernews.com/2026/11/n-able-takes-hosted-n-central-offline.html</link><guid isPermaLink="false">urn:sha256:f0d40b6eb5cac62ee86cf717f406d05317d47708def4f82c98769f895c4ecee0</guid><category>NEWS</category><chr2:sourceName>The Hacker News</chr2:sourceName><chr2:firstObservedAtJST>2026-11-10T16:22:41.134922+09:00</chr2:firstObservedAtJST><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 06:44:36 GMT</pubDate><description>N-able said it has taken N-central Hosted Environments offline and is urging on-premises customers to shut down their servers until further notice following the public disclosure of over 30 vulnerabilities collectively tracked as Able2Shell. "As a precautionary measure, we are temporarily taking our Hosted N-central environment offline while we take the necessary actions to secure the</description><chr2:heatScore>65.0</chr2:heatScore></item><item><title>Google Issues Chrome Security Update for Eighth Actively Exploited Zero-Day of 2026</ti